    "question": {
      ":question/id": "827848b3-599f-56af-84da-077d192937ab",
      ":question/problem": "![](generate/scratch/17592186059715-draft/plots/9ca4bea3bd50e7ad8f8c19b9.png)\n\nLet $A(4, -3)$ and $B(5, 5)$. Find $|\\overset{\\to }{AB}|$.",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/moderate",
      ":question/worked-solution": "We have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\overset{\\to }{OA}=a=4i-3j, \\\\ & \\overset{\\to }{OB}=b=5i+5j.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nExpressing $\\overset{\\to }{AB}$ as the difference of position vectors, we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{AB} &= \\overset{\\to }{OB}-\\overset{\\to }{OA} \\\\ &= b-a \\\\ &= (5i+5j)-(4i-3j) \\\\ &= i+8j\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe displacement components are $(5)-(4)=1$ and $(5)-(-3)=8$.\n\nNow, using the formula for the magnitude of a vector, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\overset{\\to }{AB}| &= \\sqrt{(1)^{2}+(8)^{2}} \\\\ &= \\sqrt{1+64} \\\\ &= \\sqrt{65}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
