    "question": {
      ":question/id": "2ab8ed6e-bf15-5ec9-8257-a6432f476c87",
      ":question/problem": "![](generate/scratch/17592186059715-draft/plots/f91fa443fbb0a42173a33a12.png)\n\nPoints $P$ and $Q$ are shown in the picture above. Find $|\\overset{\\to }{PQ}|$.",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/hard",
      ":question/worked-solution": "From the picture, we obtain $P(-3,-3)$ and $Q(4,6).$ So, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\overset{\\to }{OP}=p=-3i-3j, \\\\  & \\overset{\\to }{OQ}=q=4i+6j.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nExpressing $\\overset{\\to }{PQ}$ as the difference of position vectors, we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{PQ} & =\\overset{\\to }{OQ}-\\overset{\\to }{OP} \\\\  & =q-p \\\\  & =(4i+6j)-(-3i-3j) \\\\  & =7i+9j\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe displacement components are $(4)-(-3)=7$ and $(6)-(-3)=9$.\n\nNow, using the formula for the magnitude of a vector, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\overset{\\to }{PQ}| & =\\sqrt{{7}^{2}+(9)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{49+81} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{130}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      ":question/answer-fields": [
        {
          ":answer-field/id": "3e9ba68c-cba0-58b3-a8cd-3d94e78b4018",
